  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Breaking: JSON-LD output fixes (issue #42). All enumerations serialize as their schema.org/GoodRelations URI through one library-wide converter (SchemaEnumConverter); [Flags] combinations serialize as a JSON array; a member without a URI throws instead of writing a bare name or number. Enum, number and boolean properties are now nullable, so unset values are no longer written (e.g. Offer.ItemCondition, MerchantReturnPolicy fees/label sources, MonetaryAmount.MinValue/MaxValue, PriceSpecification.ValueAddedTaxIncluded, Rating.BestRating/WorstRating). schema.org URIs use https, including the default @context, which is now written on the root node only. Date-only properties (e.g. Offer.PriceValidUntil, Person.BirthDate) serialize as yyyy-MM-dd. ToJson/ToIndentedJson are virtual. Tire and Wheel no longer add hardcoded sameAs links; Wheel serializes as @type Product; Tire gets typed specs that serialize into additionalProperty. Fixed ReturnMethodEnumeration (all members wrote ReturnInStore), trailing spaces in Tuesday/DeliveryModePickUp URIs, Vehicle.SteeringPosition and Flight.EstimatedFlightDuration typed as DateTime, and TrackAction.DeliveryMethod being private. See ChangeLog.md for full details.",
